  clock: 2  # e33e
  nonce: e33e  # e33e
  set:  # e33e
    title: "Symbol.is_exported's bool default makes 'not observed' indistinguishable from 'observed false', so a non-computing producer contributes a phantom arbitration candidate"  # e33e
    fields:  # e33e
      statement: "A producer contributes a candidate for an attribute only when it OBSERVED that attribute. A field whose dataclass default is a concrete value (Symbol.is_exported: bool = False) cannot express abstention, so a producer that never computes it is indistinguishable from one that measured the default."  # e33e
      root_cause: "_empty() recognises only None/''/[] as absent, and is_exported defaults to False rather than None, so the SCIP arm — which assigns is_exported nowhere — contributes False as an observed candidate on all 169 records; the fix is a positive observed-or-not claim, not a change to arbitrate (which correctly skips empties)."  # e33e
- op: discuss  # 43de
  at: '2026-09-19T17:59:35Z'  # 43de
  by: agent  # 43de
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 43de
  clock: 3  # 43de
  nonce: 43de  # 43de
  message: "CORRECTION 2026-09-19, same day: THIS ROW AS FILED IS REFUTED, and the refutation is positive evidence read in the code and on the fixture, not a non-reproduction.\n\nWHAT I FILED: \"the incumbent's None wins arbitration over a partner's concrete value; arbitrate admits None as a candidate for every TRACKED_ATTRIBUTE.\"\n\nWHAT THE CODE DOES: `merge_producers._candidates` already skips empties before arbitration — `if _empty(value): continue  # not observed by this producer: no entry (§1)`, where `_empty(v) = v is None or v == \"\" or v == []`. An absent value is ALREADY not a candidate. §1 was implemented correctly in WI-binis.\n\nWHAT THE 41 RECORDS ACTUALLY ARE, measured on the committed aardvark-dns fixture through the merge pass: the tree-sitter arm holds is_exported=True on 41 of 148 paired records and False on the other 107; the SCIP arm holds False on all 169. So the 41 are TWO CONCRETE BOOLEANS in conflict (True vs False), and incumbent-first carried True — exactly what §4/§5 prescribe. In-memory after the merge: carried True x41, alternative False x41, attribution ('rust',) x41. There is no None anywhere in this attribute.\n\nWHY I READ IT WRONG, and it is my instrument, not the pass (LIVE.md rules 2, 4, 5): `backend_agreement` renders a disagreement's carried value with `_shape(node.get(attribute))`. `Symbol.to_dict()` serialises is_exported NESTED, under `supply_chain`, and it is the ONLY one of the ten TRACKED_ATTRIBUTES that is not a top-level key. So `node.get(\"is_exported\")` is None for every node and the table printed `null` where the real carried value is `true`. Filed as its own row against the instrument; `docs/audits/0019`'s is_exported shape column is wrong and regenerates once it is fixed (the COUNTS — 107 agree / 41 disagree — come from `attribution`/`alternatives` and are correct).\n\nRE-SCOPED RATHER THAN CLOSED, because a real defect of this family is present at a different level. `Symbol.is_exported` is declared `bool = False`, a dataclass DEFAULT, so a producer that never computes the field emits an indistinguishable observed False — the SCIP arm sets is_exported nowhere (grep: no assignment in scip/index.py or the rust-analyzer translate) yet contributes False as a CANDIDATE on all 169 records. `_empty` cannot catch it: False is not None, \"\" or []. That is this project's recurring absent-versus-empty defect at the field's type, and it makes every is_exported \"disagreement\" between a computing and a non-computing producer a phantom contest. The statement and root_cause below are rewritten to that claim. Not fixed here: the cure is a positive \"did this producer observe it\" claim (a tri-state, or per-producer observed-attribute declaration), which touches the IR and wants an owner ruling on shape."  # 43de
